IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-kleene`
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, SECTION 9: ARBITRATION PROVISIONS.
--
-- What is encoded: s 9(1) (the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement where the right is
-- subject to it) and s 9(2) (the third party who exercises a right to enforce an arbitration term is treated as a
-- party, from immediately before the exercise).  "An agreement in writing for the purposes of" the Arbitration Act
-- 2001 or Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994 is a borrowed term, asked as a fact (which of the two Acts).
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not
-- answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").

§ `Section 9(1) -- the right is subject to an arbitration term`

-- src:356 | 9.—(1) Where —
-- src:358 | (a) a right under section 2 to enforce a term (called in this
-- src:359 | section the substantive term) is subject to a term providing
-- src:360 | for the submission of disputes to arbitration (called in this
-- src:361 | section the arbitration agreement); and
-- src:363 | (b) the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the
-- src:364 | purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or Part 2 of the
-- src:365 | International Arbitration Act 1994,
-- src:367 | the third party is treated for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001
-- src:368 | or the International Arbitration Act 1994 (as the case may be) as a
-- src:369 | party to the arbitration agreement as regards disputes between the
-- src:370 | third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the
-- src:371 | substantive term by the third party.
@ref s 9(1) (src:356-371)
GIVEN `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` IS A `Arbitration statute`
      `the dispute asked about` IS A `Dispute asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the treatment is "as regards disputes between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party"; another dispute is outside it
        IF `the dispute asked about` EQUALS `any other dispute` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods-and-where ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): "Where — (a) a right under section 2 to enforce a term (called in this section the substantive term) is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration (called in this section the arbitration agreement); and (b) the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994"
        IF NOT (`the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` AND `the right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; same ruling): "(b) the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994"
        IF `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` EQUALS `neither of those` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:367 | the third party is treated for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001
-- src:368 | or the International Arbitration Act 1994 (as the case may be) as a
-- src:369 | party to the arbitration agreement as regards disputes between the
-- src:370 | third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the
-- src:371 | substantive term by the third party.
@ref s 9(1) the Act in question (src:367-371)
GIVEN `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` IS A `Arbitration statute`
      `the dispute asked about` IS A `Dispute asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Arbitration statute`
`s 9(1) the Act for the purposes of which the third party is treated as a party` MEANS
    IF `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` `the right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration` `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` `the dispute asked about` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    -- "the Arbitration Act 2001 or the International Arbitration Act 1994 (as the case may be)": the Act the agreement is in writing for
    THEN JUST `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a result that is an Act cannot carry JUST FALSE; the yes/no function above carries the "no" (assumed, not ruled: the twin of the ruling of 2026-11-05)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 9(2) -- the third party who exercises the right`

-- src:373 | (2) Where —
-- src:375 | (a) a third party has a right under section 2 to enforce a term
-- src:376 | providing for one or more descriptions of dispute between
-- src:377 | the third party and the promisor to be submitted to
-- src:378 | arbitration (called in this section the arbitration
-- src:379 | agreement);
-- src:381 | (b) the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the
-- src:382 | purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or Part 2 of the
-- src:383 | International Arbitration Act 1994; and
-- src:385 | (c) the third party does not fall to be treated under
-- src:386 | subsection (1) as a party to the arbitration agreement,
-- src:388 | the third party is, if the third party exercises the right, treated for the
-- src:389 | purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or the International Arbitration
-- src:390 | Act 1994 (as the case may be) as a party to the arbitration agreement
-- src:391 | in relation to the matter with respect to which the right is exercised,
-- src:392 | and treated as having been so immediately before the exercise of the
-- src:393 | right.
@ref s 9(2) (src:373-393)
GIVEN `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce a term providing for one or more descriptions of dispute between the third party and the promisor to be submitted to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` IS A `Arbitration statute`
      `the third party falls to be treated under subsection (1) as a party to the arbitration agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third party exercises the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time asked about` IS A `Time asked about, relative to the exercise of the right`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods-and-where ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): "Where — (a) a third party has a right under section 2 to enforce a term providing for one or more descriptions of dispute between the third party and the promisor to be submitted to arbitration; (b) the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994"
        IF NOT `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce a term providing for one or more descriptions of dispute between the third party and the promisor to be submitted to arbitration` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; same ruling): "(b) the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994"
        IF `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` EQUALS `neither of those` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; same ruling): "(c) the third party does not fall to be treated under subsection (1) as a party to the arbitration agreement"
        IF `the third party falls to be treated under subsection (1) as a party to the arbitration agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading M5): "the third party is, if the third party exercises the right, treated ... as a party to the arbitration agreement"
        IF NOT `the third party exercises the right` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the third party falls to be treated as a party under subsection (1) has not been stated
        IF `the third party falls to be treated under subsection (1) as a party to the arbitration agreement` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the third party is "treated as having been so immediately before the exercise of the right"; an earlier time is outside it
        IF `the time asked about` EQUALS `earlier than immediately before the exercise` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
